From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: sandbox-seccomp-filter: architecture of AArch64 ILP32

The ILP32 kernel reports AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64ILP32 (0xd00000b7) for AArch64 ILP32 tasks,
but configure sets AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64 for every aarch64* host, so on that kernel the
pre-auth sandbox would kill the child at its first system call and no login would work.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c
+++ b/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c
@@ -77,6 +77,15 @@
 #include "xmalloc.h"
 
 /* Linux seccomp_filter sandbox */
+/*
+ * AArch64 ILP32 tasks report AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64ILP32 on the ILP32 kernel, while
+ * configure picks AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64 for every aarch64* host.
+ */
+#if defined(__aarch64__) && defined(__ILP32__)
+# undef SECCOMP_AUDIT_ARCH
+# define SECCOMP_AUDIT_ARCH 0xd00000b7U /* AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64ILP32 */
+#endif
+
 #define SECCOMP_FILTER_FAIL SECCOMP_RET_KILL
 
 /* Use a signal handler to emit violations when debugging */
